{"id": "EUVD-2026-92017", "enisaUuid": "81689dfe-2b78-35b2-afe0-857f4673b500", "description": "Nezha Dashboard from 1.8.0 before 2.3.13 contains an improper locking vulnerability where a non-deferred mutex unlock leaks on a nil-map panic path. Any authenticated non-admin member can issue four notification API calls to permanently deadlock the alerting subsystem, then exhaust memory with blocking requests.", "datePublished": "2026-10-03T12:14:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T14:48:26", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/security/advisories/GHSA-7j7v-j77m-6g3m", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nezha-1.8.0-before-2.3.13-denial-of-service-via-notification-mutex-deadlock"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-105113", "GHSA-2w9f-mhfg-hq53"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a238c54f-bd41-3ba5-9b8e-d67e34ef0717", "product": {"name": "nezha", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}, "product_version": "1.8.0 <2.3.13"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b9483c8b-4727-30e8-a84f-9a7c9f08a471", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}], "isExploited": false}